IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `theft-nouns`
IMPORT `theft-s26-29-procedure`

-- Theft Act 1968 ss 26 to 29: tests. Layer 1.
-- Expected values were written by hand from the text of the section named beside
-- them. Yes/no fields of a fixture are FALSE unless the fixture's name says
-- otherwise. In the evidence fixtures the offence charged is always on 15 March 2020.

§ `Fixtures`

§§ `Search (s 26)`

`srch warrant to a constable` MEANS `Search facts` WITH
    `information on oath has been laid before a justice of the peace` IS TRUE
    `it has been made to appear that there is reasonable cause to believe that a person has stolen goods in his custody or possession or on his premises` IS TRUE
    `the warrant is addressed to a constable` IS TRUE
    `the warrant is addressed to someone other than a constable` IS FALSE
    `an enactment expressly provides for a warrant to be addressed to someone other than a constable` IS FALSE
    `he is authorised under section 26 to search the premises for stolen goods` IS FALSE
    `the searcher believes the goods to be stolen goods` IS FALSE
`srch warrant to another with an enactment` MEANS `Search facts` WITH
    `information on oath has been laid before a justice of the peace` IS TRUE
    `it has been made to appear that there is reasonable cause to believe that a person has stolen goods in his custody or possession or on his premises` IS TRUE
    `the warrant is addressed to a constable` IS FALSE
    `the warrant is addressed to someone other than a constable` IS TRUE
    `an enactment expressly provides for a warrant to be addressed to someone other than a constable` IS TRUE
    `he is authorised under section 26 to search the premises for stolen goods` IS FALSE
    `the searcher believes the goods to be stolen goods` IS FALSE
`srch warrant to another without an enactment` MEANS `Search facts` WITH
    `information on oath has been laid before a justice of the peace` IS TRUE
    `it has been made to appear that there is reasonable cause to believe that a person has stolen goods in his custody or possession or on his premises` IS TRUE
    `the warrant is addressed to a constable` IS FALSE
    `the warrant is addressed to someone other than a constable` IS TRUE
    `an enactment expressly provides for a warrant to be addressed to someone other than a constable` IS FALSE
    `he is authorised under section 26 to search the premises for stolen goods` IS FALSE
    `the searcher believes the goods to be stolen goods` IS FALSE
`srch no information on oath` MEANS `Search facts` WITH
    `information on oath has been laid before a justice of the peace` IS FALSE
    `it has been made to appear that there is reasonable cause to believe that a person has stolen goods in his custody or possession or on his premises` IS TRUE
    `the warrant is addressed to a constable` IS TRUE
    `the warrant is addressed to someone other than a constable` IS FALSE
    `an enactment expressly provides for a warrant to be addressed to someone other than a constable` IS FALSE
    `he is authorised under section 26 to search the premises for stolen goods` IS FALSE
    `the searcher believes the goods to be stolen goods` IS FALSE
`srch no reasonable cause` MEANS `Search facts` WITH
    `information on oath has been laid before a justice of the peace` IS TRUE
    `it has been made to appear that there is reasonable cause to believe that a person has stolen goods in his custody or possession or on his premises` IS FALSE
    `the warrant is addressed to a constable` IS TRUE
    `the warrant is addressed to someone other than a constable` IS FALSE
    `an enactment expressly provides for a warrant to be addressed to someone other than a constable` IS FALSE
    `he is authorised under section 26 to search the premises for stolen goods` IS FALSE
    `the searcher believes the goods to be stolen goods` IS FALSE
`srch authorised and believes` MEANS `Search facts` WITH
    `information on oath has been laid before a justice of the peace` IS FALSE
    `it has been made to appear that there is reasonable cause to believe that a person has stolen goods in his custody or possession or on his premises` IS FALSE
    `the warrant is addressed to a constable` IS FALSE
    `the warrant is addressed to someone other than a constable` IS FALSE
    `an enactment expressly provides for a warrant to be addressed to someone other than a constable` IS FALSE
    `he is authorised under section 26 to search the premises for stolen goods` IS TRUE
    `the searcher believes the goods to be stolen goods` IS TRUE
`srch authorised, no belief` MEANS `Search facts` WITH
    `information on oath has been laid before a justice of the peace` IS FALSE
    `it has been made to appear that there is reasonable cause to believe that a person has stolen goods in his custody or possession or on his premises` IS FALSE
    `the warrant is addressed to a constable` IS FALSE
    `the warrant is addressed to someone other than a constable` IS FALSE
    `an enactment expressly provides for a warrant to be addressed to someone other than a constable` IS FALSE
    `he is authorised under section 26 to search the premises for stolen goods` IS TRUE
    `the searcher believes the goods to be stolen goods` IS FALSE
`srch not authorised, believes` MEANS `Search facts` WITH
    `information on oath has been laid before a justice of the peace` IS FALSE
    `it has been made to appear that there is reasonable cause to believe that a person has stolen goods in his custody or possession or on his premises` IS FALSE
    `the warrant is addressed to a constable` IS FALSE
    `the warrant is addressed to someone other than a constable` IS FALSE
    `an enactment expressly provides for a warrant to be addressed to someone other than a constable` IS FALSE
    `he is authorised under section 26 to search the premises for stolen goods` IS FALSE
    `the searcher believes the goods to be stolen goods` IS TRUE

§§ `Joint handling (s 27(1), (2))`

`jh charged with others` MEANS `Joint handling facts` WITH
    `he is charged with handling all or any of the stolen goods from a theft` IS TRUE
    `others are charged in the same indictment with handling goods from the same theft, at different times or at the same time` IS TRUE
    `two or more persons are indicted for jointly handling stolen goods` IS FALSE
    `the jury are satisfied that he handled all or any of the stolen goods` IS FALSE
`jh charged alone` MEANS `Joint handling facts` WITH
    `he is charged with handling all or any of the stolen goods from a theft` IS TRUE
    `others are charged in the same indictment with handling goods from the same theft, at different times or at the same time` IS FALSE
    `two or more persons are indicted for jointly handling stolen goods` IS FALSE
    `the jury are satisfied that he handled all or any of the stolen goods` IS FALSE
`jh others charged, he is not` MEANS `Joint handling facts` WITH
    `he is charged with handling all or any of the stolen goods from a theft` IS FALSE
    `others are charged in the same indictment with handling goods from the same theft, at different times or at the same time` IS TRUE
    `two or more persons are indicted for jointly handling stolen goods` IS FALSE
    `the jury are satisfied that he handled all or any of the stolen goods` IS FALSE
`jh jointly indicted, jury satisfied` MEANS `Joint handling facts` WITH
    `he is charged with handling all or any of the stolen goods from a theft` IS FALSE
    `others are charged in the same indictment with handling goods from the same theft, at different times or at the same time` IS FALSE
    `two or more persons are indicted for jointly handling stolen goods` IS TRUE
    `the jury are satisfied that he handled all or any of the stolen goods` IS TRUE
`jh jointly indicted, jury not satisfied` MEANS `Joint handling facts` WITH
    `he is charged with handling all or any of the stolen goods from a theft` IS FALSE
    `others are charged in the same indictment with handling goods from the same theft, at different times or at the same time` IS FALSE
    `two or more persons are indicted for jointly handling stolen goods` IS TRUE
    `the jury are satisfied that he handled all or any of the stolen goods` IS FALSE
`jh not jointly indicted, jury satisfied` MEANS `Joint handling facts` WITH
    `he is charged with handling all or any of the stolen goods from a theft` IS FALSE
    `others are charged in the same indictment with handling goods from the same theft, at different times or at the same time` IS FALSE
    `two or more persons are indicted for jointly handling stolen goods` IS FALSE
    `the jury are satisfied that he handled all or any of the stolen goods` IS TRUE

