§§ `Statutory declarations (s 27(4))`

`sd good, copy given seven days before` MEANS `Statutory declaration facts` WITH
    `the proceedings are for the theft of anything in the course of transmission, or for handling stolen goods from such a theft` IS TRUE
    `the declaration says that the declarant despatched or received or failed to receive goods or a postal packet, or that they were in a particular state or condition when despatched or received` IS TRUE
    `oral evidence to the like effect would have been admissible in the proceedings` IS TRUE
    `days before the hearing or trial that a copy of the declaration was given to the person charged` IS 7
    `the person charged gave the prosecutor written notice requiring the declarant to attend` IS FALSE
    `days before the hearing or trial that he gave that notice` IS 0
    `the court allowed further time in special circumstances and he gave the notice within it` IS FALSE
