§§ `Summary trial (s 29(2))`

`st plain theft` MEANS `Summary trial facts` WITH
    `the offence is an indictable offence under the Theft Act 1968` IS TRUE
    `it is robbery, aggravated burglary, blackmail or assault with intent to rob` IS FALSE
    `it is a burglary comprising the commission of, or an intention to commit, an offence which is not included in that Schedule` IS FALSE
    `it is a burglary in a dwelling` IS FALSE
    `entry to the dwelling, or to the part of it where the burglary was committed, or to any building or part of a building containing the dwelling, was obtained by force or deception or by the use of any tool, key or appliance` IS FALSE
    `a person in the dwelling was subjected to violence or the threat of violence` IS FALSE
    `it is handling stolen goods from an offence not committed in the United Kingdom` IS FALSE
